¬import il from "../../../../../_shared/variables/imageLinks"


8. The vscode installer dialogue is displayed showing the licence agreement.

9. Click the **I accept the agreement** to enable the **Next** button. *- red ring* 

10. Then click the **Next** button. *- green ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueStart_img}}


11. The dialogue displays the **Select Destination Location** view.

12. Unless you want to install vscode somewhere other than the default location click **Next**. *- red ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueLocation_img}}


13. The dialogue displays the **Select Start Menu Folder** view.

14. Click **Next**. *- red ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueLocation_img}}


15. The dialogue displays the **Select Additional Tasks** view.

16. If they are not already selected select the following - they make opening files from File Explorer easier: *- red ring* 
    - **Add "Open with Code" action to Windows Explorer file context menu**
    - **Add "Open with Code" action to Windows Explorer directory context menu**

17. Click **Next**. *- green ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueTasks_img}}

18. The installation will take a couple of minutes and when finished dialogue displays the **Ready to Install** view.

19. Click **Install**. *- green ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueSummary_img}}


20. The installation will take a couple of minutes and when finished dialogue displays the following view.

21. If the checkbox **Launch Visual Studio Code** is checked then vscode is launched when you click the **Finish** button. *- green ring* 

22. Click **Finish** button. *- red ring* 

{{::il.Vscode_InstallDialogueCompleted_img}}


23. If the checkbox **Launch Visual Studio Code** was checked vscode launches. 

{{::il.Vscode_FreshlyInstalled_img}}

